⚠️ **IMPORTANT: unguarded `errorTicketKeyOf(params)` in `action()`'s catch — a falsy `params` now throws out of the catch instead of failing gracefully**

Every other error-path call site of `errorTicketKeyOf` is wrapped in try/catch (`handleActionError` at js/pushReworkChanges.js:2851–2869, `reportActionError` in js/preCliReworkSetup.js) precisely so the catch can never throw. This new call in front of `handleActionError` breaks that pattern:

```javascript
} catch (error) {
    postCompletionTokenUsage(params, errorTicketKeyOf(params));   // ← throws when params is falsy
    return handleActionError(params, error, tracker);
}
```

`errorTicketKeyOf` dereferences `params.ticket` unguarded (js/pushReworkChanges.js:2811). When `action(undefined)`/`action(null)` reaches this catch (the first throw comes from `actionSetup` at line 2894, so the catch is guaranteed to run with the same falsy `params`), this line raises a fresh TypeError from inside the catch block. On `main` the identical scenario returns `{ success: false, error: ... }` because `handleActionError` guards the same lookup — the PR turns a graceful failure into a thrown exception, and `handleActionError`/`postReworkErrorComment` become unreachable for it.

Suggested fix (keeps gh-1521's guarantee while staying crash-proof like `postTokenUsageSafely`):

```javascript
} catch (error) {
    var usageKey = null;
    try { usageKey = errorTicketKeyOf(params); } catch (eKey) { /* keep null */ }
    postCompletionTokenUsage(params, usageKey);
    return handleActionError(params, error, tracker);
}
```

